Node InsertCDLL(Node head, int x) {
    Node temp = new Node(x);               // Create new node with data x
    if (head == null) {                    // If list is empty
        temp.next = temp;                  // New node points to itself (next)
        temp.prev = temp;                  // New node points to itself (prev)
        return temp;                       // Return new node as head
    }
    temp.next = head;                      // New node's next → head
    temp.prev = head.prev;                 // New node's prev → last node
    head.prev.next = temp;                 // Last node's next → new node
    head.prev = temp;                      // Head's prev → new node
    return temp;                           // Return new node as new head
}


//////////////////////// DRY RUN ////////////////////

List: 10 ↔ 20 ↔ 30 (circular), Insert x = 5 at beginning

INITIAL:
        (head)
          │
          ▼
    [10|•|•] ↔ [20|•|•] ↔ [30|•|•]
      ▲                       │
      └───────────────────────┘

STEP 1: temp = [5|•|•]

STEP 2: temp.next = head
[5|•|•] → [10|•|•]

STEP 3: temp.prev = head.prev (30)
[30|•|•] ← [5|•|•] → [10|•|•]

STEP 4: head.prev.next = temp (30.next → 5)
[30|•|•] → [5|•|•] → [10|•|•]

STEP 5: head.prev = temp (10.prev → 5)

FINAL:
        (new head)
            │
            ▼
    [5|•|•] ↔ [10|•|•] ↔ [20|•|•] ↔ [30|•|•]
      ▲                                       │
      └───────────────────────────────────────┘

Result: 5 ↔ 10 ↔ 20 ↔ 30 (circular)


//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Insert at Beginning of Circular Doubly Linked List

Input : 10 ↔ 20 ↔ 30 (circular), x = 5
Output: 5 ↔ 10 ↔ 20 ↔ 30 (circular, head = 5)

Input : null (empty list), x = 7
Output: 7 (single node circular, head = 7)

Edge Cases:
1. Empty list → new node points to itself, return it
2. Single node → insert before it, both form 2-node circle
3. Multiple nodes → insert between last and first, update 4 links

Constraints:
• 0 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 10⁵
• 1 ≤ x ≤ 10⁵

TC: O(1) | SC: O(1)

Note: Original code has 2 bugs:
- Line `temp.next = head` overwrites `temp.next = head.prev`
- Line `head.prev.next = temp` uses updated head.prev (which is temp)
Fix: Store last node reference or reorder assignments as shown above.
